    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Manager-authorized temporary constraint relaxation with mandatory monitoring: The production manager may authorize a one-cycle, time-bounded relaxation of both constraints: FatigueIndex ceiling raised from 0.40 to 0.50 (still below the 0.60 clinical alert threshold) and Noise ceiling raised from 80.0 dB to 83.0 dB (with mandatory PPE enforcement and continuous sound-level monitoring). This option partially meets demand but does NOT preserve the original human-centric constraint thresholds. Authorization must be logged with a justification record in the CBPA governance ledger, a return-to-compliance plan filed within 48 hours, and occupational health notified. This option should not be selected in consecutive planning cycles without a formal constraint review.
      Preserves human constraints: No

